WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.935
LARRY ARNN: Watch a
horse go backwards.

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.060
It's not very good at that.

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:05.190
If you can see
that about a horse,

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:06.870
you can see it about a person.

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:09.310
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYS]

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.580
For a provisional
explanation, we'll

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:20.160
use the term "good" to mean "a
thing being fully what it is."

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.390
That's a good glass.

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:23.850
I don't think it's a great one.

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.500
It's not to my taste, anyway.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:26.775
But it's fine.

00:00:26.775 --> 00:00:27.900
It functions.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.420
If you drilled a hole
in the bottom of it,

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.330
wouldn't be a good
glass anymore.

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:34.080
I was blessed with a
really great teacher.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.710
And one of the best things he
understood and could explain--

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:39.930
he knew his Aristotle--
was how does it come

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:43.320
to be that we use common nouns?

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:44.340
How can we do that?

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:49.560
Let's see, here-- no.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:51.480
Everything's too uniform
around here, right?

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:54.240
So pen, pen, right?

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:55.560
They're different.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:57.390
How do you know?

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.400
And yet, you know.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.350
You can say to somebody
in another room, where

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:04.050
neither of you can see what
you're instructing the person

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:08.682
to do, would you please go
and get me a pen on my desk?

00:01:08.682 --> 00:01:10.140
And they got no
idea what the thing

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:13.440
is going to look like
when they get there.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:14.990
But they always find it.

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:17.600
This is light work
for human beings.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:19.610
This is automatic.

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:22.190
And nobody ever
teaches us to do it.

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:25.790
When we're about two years old,
we all start talking, right?

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:28.490
And no other being ever does.

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:29.960
We have four children.

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:32.330
We didn't teach them to talk.

00:01:32.330 --> 00:01:33.830
They just started talking.

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:36.260
In our family, the
children are raised just

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:38.090
like the dogs for
the first two years.

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:41.990
Live on the floor, eat the
food on the floor, you know.

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:45.320
But then they start talking.

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:47.480
Somehow they can do that.

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:49.730
And the dogs never do, right?

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:51.258
They're still stupid.

00:01:51.258 --> 00:01:52.550
That's their charm, by the way.

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:53.050
[CHUCKLES]

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:58.340
So Aristotle says
that's how we see good.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:01.160
Things are defined
by their purpose.

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:04.370
And the point is,
this does this.

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:05.960
And this is a fine point, right?

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:06.240
STUDENT: Yeah.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:06.500
LARRY ARNN: Yeah.

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:07.833
You're a very precise young man.

00:02:07.833 --> 00:02:12.470
And so the point
is, it does this.

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:17.885
And this-- that's
yours-- this does this.

00:02:20.843 --> 00:02:22.760
And this does the same
thing, except it's hot.

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:25.970
And it's got a little cool
magnetic top on the top.

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:28.670
So that's their purpose.

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:34.040
They're good at it.

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:38.720
They become hard to recognize
if they're harmed in a way that

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.010
defeats the purpose.

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:42.350
The good and the being,
Aristotle writes,

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:45.860
are convertible terms, where
you can use one in a sentence,

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:47.180
you can use the other one.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:48.830
Good cup, being of the cup.

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:51.500
Good book, being
of the book, right?

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:55.250
Good glasses, being
of the glasses.

00:02:55.250 --> 00:03:00.650
The basis of all human
speech is the common noun.

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:03.470
And every time we
identify one, we

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:07.010
are identifying the good
and the being of a thing.

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:09.830
Horses love to run.

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:12.200
And they're beautiful
when they run.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:17.360
And so their ability to do that,
that's what's awesome, right?

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:21.380
If you think that the word
"education" means lead forth,

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:24.770
watch a horse go forward.

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:27.360
And then watch it go backwards.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:28.890
It's not very good at that.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:33.020
Well, the point is, if you
can see that about a horse,

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:36.830
you can see it about
a person, you see.

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:40.010
And then Aristotle
is going to say--

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:42.890
before we're done--
that if you practice up

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:46.790
through these immediate
and sometimes small

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:51.740
virtues every day in a way
to build your character,

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:54.520
those people become good.

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:58.720
Human beings, we're going
to discover, face obstacles.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:05.250
And the virtues are the good
confrontation and tackling

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:06.960
of those obstacles.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:13.890
And if you do that, it will
change you and make you better.

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:15.750
You can become awesome.

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:16.560
Start today.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:18.980
[CLASSIC MUSIC PLAYS]

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:22.720
I am Larry Arnn, president
of Hillsdale College.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:25.210
You will find, if you look
at our online courses,

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:27.820
that they cover the whole
range of human learning,

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:31.300
all the high and fundamental
things everyone needs to know.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.580
They are free,
because we have always

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:36.550
wished to provide sound
learning to anyone

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:38.880
who wishes to have it.

